<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea sells dollars again at 870.00.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea sells dollars again at 870.00.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea stepped into late afternoon interbank trading for the second time on Friday to sell dollars as the won fell to the 870.00 level, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank has refused to confirm or deny that it intervenes in the market.  </p>
<p>The won rose to 869.50 just after the intervention.</p>
<p>Dealers said the dollar's bullish trend would be difficult to stem due to the widening trade deficit and the U.S. unit's strong trend against the Japanese yen on world markets.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
